Why Playwright?

Playwright is an open-source automation framework developed by Microsoft for web/UI automation and end-to-end testing.

Basic Features

1. Built-in Auto-Waiting Capability
		Playwright automatically waits for elements to become ready before performing actions.
		This reduces the need to write explicit waits such as fixed sleep statements.
2. Built-in Actionability Checks
		Before performing an action, Playwright automatically checks whether the element is:
			Visible
			Stable
			Able to receive the required event
			Enabled
			Editable, when applicable
		This helps make tests more reliable.
3. Cross-Browser Support
		Playwright supports the major browser engines:
			Chromium
			Firefox
			WebKit
	Chromium-based browsers include Chrome and Microsoft Edge.
4. Multi-Platform Support
		Playwright can be used on:
			Windows
			macOS
			Linux
5. Multi-Language Support
		Playwright provides support for:
			JavaScript
			TypeScript
			Python
			Java
			C# / .NET
			
Advanced Features

1. Tracing and Debugging
		Playwright provides a powerful tracing mechanism for debugging tests.
		Trace information can include:
			Screenshots
			DOM snapshots
			Network activity
			Test actions
			Console information
		Playwright also supports video recording when configured.
2. Network Interception
		Playwright can intercept and modify network requests and responses.
		We can mock API responses and provide static/test data.
		This is useful when testing UI behavior without depending on the actual backend API.
3. Browser Context Management
		Playwright uses isolated browser contexts.
		Each context behaves like a separate browser session.
		We can save and reuse authentication/storage state such as cookies and local storage.
		This is useful for avoiding repeated login steps.
4. Codegen Tool
		Playwright Codegen can record actions performed in the browser and generate corresponding Playwright code.
		It can be useful for quickly creating an initial test script.

