const and let in JavaScript/TypeScript

In JavaScript, const and let are used to declare variables.

const

Use const when the variable should not be reassigned.

const context = await browser.newContext();
const page = await context.newPage();

Here, context and page cannot be reassigned to another value later.

For example:

const page = await context.newPage();
page = anotherPage; // ❌ Not allowed
---------------------------------------------------
let

Use let when the variable needs to be reassigned.

let page = await context.newPage();
page = anotherPage; // ✅ Allowed

Important Correction

Instead of writing:

"In JS, the return type of the variable is Let/Const"

write:

let and const are JavaScript keywords used to declare variables. They are not return types.

Example: const page = await context.newPage();

